<title>MEXICO: Banacci up on unit sale rumours - traders.</title>
<headline>Banacci up on unit sale rumours - traders.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Grupo Financiero Banamex-Accival (Banacci) were up sharply Wednesday on rumours the financial group is to announce a partial or complete sell-off of its stake in an Argentine bank, traders said.</p>
<p>The rumour surrounds Banacci's holding in Grupo Banesto-Banco Shaw. Banacci B shares were up 1.16 pesos to 18.76 pesos.</p>
<p>&quot;The stock is in demand, they're buying on a rumor of divesting in their Argentine interest,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Analysts, however, said they thought the stock's upward charge was on fundamentals.</p>
</text>
